    "question": "It takes Jennifer 20 minutes to groom each of her 2 long hair dachshunds.  If she grooms her dogs every day, how many hours does she spend grooming her dogs in 30 days?",
    "gold": "20",
    "answer": "She has 2 dogs and it takes 20 minutes to groom just 1 dog so it takes her 2*20 = <<2*20=40>>40 minutes per day to groom 2 dogs\nIn 30 days, she will have spent 30*40 = <<30*40=1200>>1,200 minutes grooming her dogs\nThere are 60 minutes in an hour so she spends 1200/60 = <<1200/60=20>>20 hours grooming her dogs\n#### 20"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many hours Jennifer spends grooming her dogs in 30 days, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total time Jennifer spends grooming her dogs in one day.\n2. Multiply the daily grooming time by the number of days to find the total time spent in 30 days.\n3. Convert the total time from minutes to hours.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total time spent grooming in one day.\nJennifer has 2 long hair dachshunds, and it takes her 20 minutes to groom each dog. Therefore, the time spent grooming one dog is 20 minutes. For 2 dogs, the total time is:\n\\[ 20 \\text{ minutes/dog} \\times 2 \\text{ dogs} = 40 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate the total time spent grooming in 30 days.\nSince Jennifer grooms her dogs every day, the total time spent grooming in 30 days is:\n\\[ 40 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 30 \\text{ days} = 1200 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nStep 3: Convert the total time from minutes to hours.\nThere are 60 minutes in an hour, so we convert 1200 minutes to hours by dividing by 60:\n\\[ 1200 \\text{ minutes} \\div 60 \\text{ minutes/hour} = 20 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total time Jennifer spends grooming her dogs in 30 days is \\(\\boxed{20}\\) hours.",
